lead-crm/*
# Track the CRM python tooling so fixes travel between clones; lead data,
# ledgers and health snapshots stay out of git. A bare "lead-crm/" exclusion
# would stop git descending into the directory at all, making any "!*.py"
# negation below unreachable -- hence the /* form plus the re-included subdirs.
# Deny-by-default is deliberate: an allowlist of known data files (leads,
# ledgers, drafts) silently leaks each new data file someone adds.
!lead-crm/*.py
!lead-crm/*/
lead-crm/*/*
!lead-crm/*/*.py
